WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.704
An agent fixes a typo, then
tries to force push to main.

2
00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.701
Guardrail stops it, and asks you first.

3
00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.160
You say no, and it tells you so.

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:14.373
Let's ship a feature with pi extensions.

5
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:21.432
You type five commands: plan,
workflow, review, ship, and retro.

6
00:00:21.432 --> 00:00:26.873
And underneath every step, there
are guards you never have to call.

7
00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:32.477
Start with slash plan. The agent
can read, but it can't edit.

8
00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:35.576
When a decision is really yours, it asks.

9
00:00:35.576 --> 00:00:39.808
Then it writes the plan,
including how it'll be checked.

10
00:00:39.808 --> 00:00:42.907
And nothing changes until you approve it.

11
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.827
Slash until gives it a finish line.

12
00:00:52.827 --> 00:00:58.608
Here it says it's done, but the test
still fails, so it's sent straight back.

13
00:00:58.608 --> 00:01:01.160
It only stops when the tests pass.

14
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:10.338
Now, a guard you never see. The
agent says done, without checking.

15
00:01:10.338 --> 00:01:12.995
Done gate quietly reminds the model,

16
00:01:12.995 --> 00:01:17.867
so it runs the repo's own verify
script before it claims anything.

17
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.014
Slash review looks for real
defects, not style notes.

18
00:01:25.014 --> 00:01:29.832
It runs the command line, and catches
a bug the unit test can't reach.

19
00:01:29.832 --> 00:01:33.687
Ask for the fix, and it proves
it with the same command.

20
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:45.997
Slash ship checks again, commits only
the files it should, and pushes once.

21
00:01:45.997 --> 00:01:49.806
Guardrail still asks, and
this time, you say yes.

22
00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:53.927
And it's honest: passing
locally isn't passing on CI.

23
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:04.085
Six guards run underneath it all: guardrail,
done gate, diagnosis nudge, drift,

24
00:02:04.085 --> 00:02:08.031
deslop, and the router.
You never call them.

25
00:02:08.031 --> 00:02:11.080
They're simply on, for every step.

26
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
pi extensions. Clone it, reload, and ship.
